# Last Shift
Category: Digital Forensics 
Level of Difficulty: Medium - Hard

An employee was recently terminated after a routine audit revealed unusual activity shortly before departure from the organization.

The incident response team recovered a small collection of digital artifacts from the employee's workstation, including network traffic captures, 
browser activity records, memory remnants and a suspicious image file.

Initial analysis suggests that sensitive information may have been collected, encrypted and prepared for exfiltration. 

Your task is to perform a forensic investigation of the provided evidence, reconstruct the employee's actions and determine what information was ultimately hidden. 
The evidence has been intentionally fragmented across multiple artifacts. 
A successful investigation will require correlating findings from different sources rather than relying on a single file. 

Recover the final flag. 

